{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-22886","model_call":2,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ undocumented \"illegal immigrants\" unauthorized) (+ medicaid medicare) (+ eligible eligibility ineligible) (+ emergency coverage))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ undocumented \"illegal immigrants\" unauthorized) (+ medicaid medicare) (+ eligible eligibility ineligible) (+ emergency coverage))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_280187894#0_581027596","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1360","rank":1,"snippet":"headings\": \"II. Medicaid for Undocumented Immigrants with PRUCOL Status II. Medicaid for Undocumented Immigrants with PRUCOL Status Medicaid for Undocumented Immigrants with PRUCOL Status Who is Eligible? How Do I Apply? Share this: Cancel reply \" , \"segment\": \"II. Medicaid for Undocumented Immigrants with PRUCOL Status | Medical Deportation II. Medicaid for Undocumented Immigrants with PRUCOL Status Medicaid for Undocumented Immigrants with PRUCOL Status Download a PDF version of our PRUCOL fact sheet here. Most undocumented immigrants are ineligible for Medicaid. However, in various states around the country, some <cover>undocumented immigrants may be eligible for full Medicaid coverage </cover>if they meet the conditions for PRUCOL status. PRUCOL persons are undocumented immigrants who are “ P ermanently R esiding U nder C olor o f L aw.” PRUCOL is not an immigration status or a path to citizenship; rather, it is a public benefits eligibility category through which certain undocumented immigrants can apply for Medicaid. New York is one such state that provides full Medicaid coverage to PRUCOL-eligible persons. In 1997, the state of New York implemented federal welfare reform that restricted Medicaid eligibility for lawfully-residing undocumented immigrants for Medicaid eligibility.\" , \""},"time":1899},"model_calls":2,"document_judgments":1,"relevance_3":0,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
