{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-22886","model_call":10,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ undocumented \"illegal immigrants\") (+ healthcare.gov marketplace \"health insurance\") (+ eligible ineligible eligibility) (+ medicaid subsidies))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ undocumented \"illegal immigrants\") (+ healthcare.gov marketplace \"health insurance\") (+ eligible ineligible eligibility) (+ medicaid subsidies))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1653084586#4_3432837778","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1363","rank":1,"snippet":"residents who are not eligible for Medicaid and do not have an affordable offer of ESI; subsidies for marketplace coverage are available to people with family income between 100% and 400% of poverty. Some people who lose ESI may be newly-eligible for income-based subsidies, based on other family income plus any state and new federal unemployment benefit received (including the $600 per week federal supplement, unlike for Medicaid). 2 While current income is used for Medicaid eligibility, annual income for the calendar year is used for marketplace subsidy eligibility. Advance subsidies are available based on estimated annual income, but the subsidies are reconciled based on actual income on the tax return filed the following year. People who lose ESI due to job loss qualify for a special enrollment period (SEP) for marketplace coverage. 3 As with <cover>Medicaid, undocumented immigrants are ineligible for marketplace </cover>coverage or subsidies.\" , \"start_char\": 3469.000000 , \"title\": \"Eligibility for ACA Health Coverage Following Job Loss | KFF\" , \"url\": \"https://www.kff.org/coronavirus-covid-19/issue-brief/eligibility-for-aca-health-coverage-following-job-loss/\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1653084586#4_3432837778","rank":1,"relevance":2}]},"time":1158},"model_calls":10,"document_judgments":9,"relevance_3":5,"max_do