{"actor":"model","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-22886","model_call":20,"attempt":1,"model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input_tokens":10298,"output_tokens":227,"total_tokens":10525,"cached_tokens":9472,"reasoning_tokens":22},"output_characters":977,"decision":{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1653338202#0_3433220061","relevance":3,"reason":"The KFF issue brief is dedicated to health coverage and care for undocumented immigrants and directly states they have limited coverage options, are barred from Medicare, Medicaid, CHIP, and ACA Marketplaces, may obtain limited low-cost care at community health centers, and must receive emergency screening/stabilization under federal law with Medicaid offsetting some hospital costs.","learned":"Undocumented immigrants generally do not get broad free public healthcare; they are barred from major federal coverage programs, though emergency care must be provided and some low-cost community health center care may be available."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1368","reason":"This focused KFF query produced a highly relevant dedicated document; continue to find more direct passages or additional sources on undocumented immigrants' health coverage and emergency Medicaid."}}}
