{"actor":"model","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-22886","model_call":21,"attempt":1,"model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input_tokens":10817,"output_tokens":340,"total_tokens":11157,"cached_tokens":9984,"reasoning_tokens":143},"output_characters":1014,"decision":{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_479997533#4_985530832","relevance":3,"reason":"This Reuters fact-check segment is dedicated to the claim that undocumented immigrants get healthcare for free and directly explains exceptions: some states use state-only funds for certain undocumented groups, emergency treatment must be provided regardless of immigration status, but undocumented immigrants are generally excluded from Medicare/ACA marketplaces and face major barriers to care.","learned":"Some state/local programs cover limited undocumented groups, and emergency treatment is required regardless of status; otherwise undocumented immigrants are generally excluded from major federal health coverage programs and many remain uninsured."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1368","reason":"The KFF-focused query is producing highly relevant documents and passages about undocumented immigrants' health coverage, emergency care, Medicaid, and whether care is free; continue while it remains productive."}}}
