{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-22886","model_call":42,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1378"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1378"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1529612638#6_3106551014","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1378","rank":2,"snippet":"7438.000000 , \"headings\": \"How Do Immigrants Obtain Health Insurance Under the ACA? How Do Immigrants Obtain Health Insurance Under the ACA? Some Different Rules Apply for Medicaid and for Premium Subsidies Are ACA Premium Subsidies Limited to U.S. Citizens? How Does the Exchange Know That Applicants Are Lawfully Present? What Coverage Is Available for Immigrants Who Are 65 or Older? Can an Immigrant Enroll in Coverage Outside of Open Enrollment?<cover>Can Undocumented Immigrants Obtain Coverage? \" , \"segment\": \"Before 2014, there were few options for recent immigrants aged 65 or older. Private individual health insurance policies generally weren't available for anyone over the age of 64, and like Medicaid, </cover>there's a five-year wait before recent immigrants can enroll in Medicare. So older immigrants often had to rely on long-term travel insurance, unless they had access to an employer-sponsored plan in the U.S. Even after five years, Medicare was often unaffordable for immigrants. Since Medicare is partially funded by payroll taxes that U.S. workers pay during their careers, Medicare Part A (hospital insurance) is only premium-free for people who have paid "},"time":9},"model_calls":42,"document_judgments":37,"relevance_3":20,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
